<main>
<p class="kicker">HFT Practice · Lesson 0038</p>
<h1>The GUI, and the Three Ways to Run a Trading Method (like the 2-Candle)</h1>
<div class="why"><strong>Why this matters:</strong> "run the 2-candle strategy" means
three different things in this codebase depending on the engine you pick — and the
desktop GUI, which predates the strategies package, runs none of them. Knowing which
door leads where saves you from hunting the GUI for a button that doesn't exist.</div>

<h2 id="s1">1 · The mental model: one pattern, three engines</h2>
<p>The <em>pattern</em> (bullish/bearish engulfing — a red candle whose body is
swallowed by the next green one, or vice versa) is defined exactly once, in
<code>strategies/engulfing.py</code>. Three engines can drive it:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Engine</th><th>Command</th><th>Bar frequency</th><th>Exit logic</th><th>Persists?</th></tr>
<tr><td>Intraday PaperEngine</td><td><code>intraday-sim</code></td><td>1m–60m bars</td><td>Stop-loss / take-profit / forced end-of-day close</td><td>CSV files per run</td></tr>
<tr><td>Arena backtest</td><td><code>arena-run backtest</code></td><td>Daily</td><td>One-bar hold, next close</td><td>Verdict in arena.db</td></tr>
<tr><td>Arena live</td><td><code>arena-run live</code></td><td>Daily</td><td>One-bar hold, next close</td><td>Ongoing ledger in arena.db</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The GUI is a <em>fourth</em> thing entirely: a Tkinter front-end over the
<strong>GBM/mean-variance pipeline</strong> (train, walk-forward, news, universe,
execution, metrics). It was built before <code>strategies/</code> existed and has no
engulfing/arena tabs.</p>

<h2 id="s2">2 · The GUI tour</h2>
<pre><code>uv run gui-hft     <span class="cm"># Docker users: MPLBACKEND=Agg is already set in docker-compose.yml</span></code></pre>
<p><span class="path">gui_app.py — class App(tk.Tk), six ttk.Notebook tabs</span>
Each tab is a form wrapped around one CLI's functionality, run on a background
thread so the window doesn't freeze:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Tab</th><th>Wraps</th><th>What you do there</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Walkforward</strong></td><td><code>walkforward-sim</code></td><td>Pick a .joblib bundle + tickers file + dates, optionally pre-download OHLCV, hit <em>Run Walkforward</em></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Train/Backtest</strong></td><td><code>paper-backtest</code></td><td>Train the GBM and save the bundle (<em>Run Backtest + Save Model</em>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Universe Builder</strong></td><td><code>universe-builder</code></td><td>Scrape S&amp;P 500 / NASDAQ ticker lists into <code>tickers/</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>News</strong></td><td><code>news-fetch</code> / <code>news-features</code></td><td>Pull Alpha Vantage sentiment, engineer features (needs <code>ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Execution</strong></td><td><code>rh-exec</code></td><td>Predict + allocate + (dry-run) submit. The <em>"Dry run (no orders)"</em> checkbox defaults to CHECKED — unticking it is the GUI's real-money gate</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Analyze Equity</strong></td><td><code>analyze-equity</code></td><td>Point at any equity CSV, get Sharpe/CAGR/MaxDD</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Rule of thumb: anything the GUI does, the CLI does too (the tabs call the same
functions) — but not the reverse. Strategies, the arena, stress tests, SHAP, and
drift checks are CLI-only today.</p>

<h2 id="s3">3 · Running the 2-candle, both ways</h2>
<h3>Intraday, with stops (the PaperEngine path)</h3>
<pre><code>uv run intraday-sim --tickers AAPL,MSFT --start 2026-06-20 \
    --interval 5m --strategy engulfing \
    --position_dollars 1000 --stop_loss_pct 0.005 --take_profit_pct 0.01
<span class="cm"># outputs equity.csv + trades.csv; --no_short to go long-only
# intervals: 1m 5m 15m 30m 60m — yfinance only serves ~7 days of 1m bars</span></code></pre>
<p>Mechanics (<code>strategies/paper_engine.py</code>): a signal on bar N enters at bar
N+1's open; each later bar checks stop-loss first (it wins ties with take-profit);
any open position force-closes on the day's last bar — never hold overnight.</p>

<h3>Daily, in the arena (screen → live → compare)</h3>
<pre><code>uv run arena-run backtest --start 2023-01-01 --end 2025-01-01 \
    --strategies engulfing            <span class="cm"># or engulfing,technical,meanrev</span>
uv run arena-run live                 <span class="cm"># daily tick; breaker + divergence watching</span>
uv run arena-run report</code></pre>
<p>Same pattern code, adapted to daily bars by
<code>strategies/candlestick_daily.py</code> (last two daily candles). One behavioral
difference to expect: the regime gate keeps engulfing out of <em>trending</em>
markets — a reversal pattern is a mean-reversion bet, so on trending days it holds
by design (disable with <code>--no_regime_gate</code> to experiment).</p>

<h2 id="s4">4 · Often confused</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Pair</th><th>The difference</th></tr>
<tr><td>GUI Execution tab vs <code>rh-exec</code></td><td>Same engine — the tab is a form over the executor. Both default to dry-run; the checkbox and <code>--no_dry_run</code> are the same gate wearing two outfits.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>intraday-sim</code> engulfing vs arena engulfing</td><td>Identical pattern detector, different worlds: 5-minute bars with SL/TP/EOD exits vs daily bars with one-bar holds, costs, sizing, and watchdogs. Their results are NOT comparable to each other.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Train/Backtest tab vs Walkforward tab</td><td>Train/Backtest fits the model once on a single split (optimistic, produces the bundle); Walkforward replays history without ever training on the traded day (honest validation). Lesson 0037's rule: validate with the second.</td></tr>
<tr><td>"strategy" in <code>intraday-sim --strategy</code> vs arena <code>--strategies</code></td><td>Two separate registries: intraday_sim.STRATEGIES (intraday contract, engulfing only today) vs strategies/registry.py (daily contract: engulfing, technical, meanrev, gbm).</td></tr>
</table>

