<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q2.</strong> In an intraday-sim run, a bar triggers BOTH the stop-loss and the take-profit. What happens?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Optimistic and wrong — the engine is deliberately conservative on ambiguous bars.">Take-profit wins — you get the gain</li>
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="PaperEngine checks stop-loss first by design: when a bar's range spans both exits you can't know which hit first, so the engine assumes the worse outcome.">Stop-loss wins — the engine assumes the worse fill</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Positions do force-close at end of day, but that's a separate rule for the day's LAST bar.">The position rides until end of day</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="No averaging — one exit fires, and it's the pessimistic one.">The two exits average out</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="feedback" hidden></p>
</div>

<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q3.</strong> Arena-run live shows engulfing holding on a day when you can SEE a textbook engulfing pattern on the chart. Most likely reason?</p>
  <ul class="options">
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="The daily adapter delegates to the exact same detector that flagged your chart pattern.">The daily adapter uses a different pattern definition</li>
    <li data-correct="true" data-why="The regime gate: engulfing's compatible_regimes is {mean_reverting, neutral}, so on a day classified as trending (or high_vol) it holds no matter what the candles say. Check the regime_log table, or rerun with --no_regime_gate.">That day's market regime was classified trending/high_vol, so the gate held it out</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="PAUSED would show in the report and it would skip the strategy entirely, not just one day.">The circuit breaker paused it</li>
    <li data-correct="false" data-why="Doji filtering exists, but a 'textbook' engulfing implies real bodies — and it wouldn't explain regime-correlated holds.">Both candles were dojis</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="feedback" hidden></p>
</div>

<div class="question" data-question>
  <p><strong>Q4.</strong> Why does <code>--interval 1m</code> only work for recent dates?</p>
  <ul class="options">
