<h2 id="s6">6 · Check your understanding (scenarios)</h2>
<div class="scenario"><details><summary><strong>Scenario A.</strong> You want to know whether the 2-candle works better with tighter stops. Which engine, which flags, and what do you compare?</summary>
<p>Intraday engine — stops only exist there. Two runs differing only in
<code>--stop_loss_pct</code> (e.g. 0.005 vs 0.003), same tickers/dates/interval,
distinct <code>--out_csv</code> names, then <code>analyze-equity --equity_csv</code> on each.
The arena can't answer this: its daily one-bar hold has no stop-loss concept.</p></details></div>
<div class="scenario"><details><summary><strong>Scenario B.</strong> Your friend wants to try the platform but is command-line-averse. What CAN you honestly give them via the GUI, and where's the line?</summary>
<p>The full GBM lifecycle: train a model (Train/Backtest), validate it (Walkforward),
build ticker lists, pull news, compute metrics, and even dry-run executions — all
point-and-click. The line: anything strategy-arena related (2-candle, technical,
meanrev, ensembles, breaker, reports) is CLI-only today. A GUI arena tab would be a
reasonable future issue.</p></details></div>
<div class="scenario"><details><summary><strong>Scenario C.</strong> intraday-sim's engulfing made money last week but the arena's engulfing is EXCLUDED. Contradiction?</summary>
<p>No — different games. Intraday: 5-minute bars, SL/TP risk control, flat overnight.
Arena: daily bars, one-bar holds, transaction costs, screened over years of history.
A pattern can have intraday edge and no daily edge (or vice versa). The two results
answer different questions and neither invalidates the other.</p></details></div>

<script>
function shuffle(arr){
  for (let i = arr.length - 1; i > 0; i--){
    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
    [arr[i], arr[j]] = [arr[j], arr[i]];
  }
  return arr;
}
let answered = 0, right = 0;
document.querySelectorAll('[data-question]').forEach(q => {
  const list = q.querySelector('.options');
  shuffle([...list.children]).forEach(li => list.appendChild(li));
  const feedback = q.querySelector('.feedback');
  let done = false;
  list.querySelectorAll('li').forEach(li => {
    li.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const correct = li.dataset.correct === 'true';
      if (!done){ answered++; if (correct) right++; done = true; }
      li.classList.add(correct ? 'picked-right' : 'picked-wrong');
      feedback.hidden = false;
      feedback.textContent = (correct ? '✓ Correct. ' : '✗ Not quite. ') + li.dataset.why;
      feedback.style.color = correct ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)';
      document.getElementById('score').textContent = right + ' / ' + answered;
    });
  });
});
</script>
